[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:A Noble Gift]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.70]Where was the Statue of Liberty made? | 自由女神像是在哪里制造的？
[00:15.67]One of the most famous monuments in the world, the Statue of Liberty, | 世界上最著名的纪念碑之一——自由女神像，
[00:21.58]was presented to the USA in the nineteenth century by the people of France. | 是法国人民在19世纪送给美国的。
[00:29.30]The great statue, which was designed by the sculptor Auguste Bartholdi, took ten years to complete. | 这座巨大的雕像是雕塑家奥古斯特·巴托尔迪设计的，花了10年时间才完成。
[00:39.14]The actual figure was made of copper supported by a metal framework which had been especially constructed by Eiffel. | 雕像的实体用铜制成，由埃菲尔特别建造的金属框架支撑着。
[00:49.09]Before it could be transported to the United States, | 在把它运往美国之前，
[00:53.21]a site had to be found for it and a pedestal had to be built. | 必须先给它选好场地，还要建造一个基座。
[00:58.79]The site chosen was an island at the entrance of New York Harbour. | 选定的场址是纽约港入口处的一个岛。
[01:04.37]By 1884, a statue which was 151 feet tall had been erected in Paris. | 到1884年，一座高达151英尺的雕像在巴黎竖立起来了。
[01:13.43]The following year, it was taken to pieces and sent to America. | 第二年，它被拆成小块运到了美国。
[01:19.43]By the end of October 1886, | 到1886年10月底，
[01:23.80]the statue had been put together again and it was officially presented to the American people by Bartholdi. | 雕像重新组装完毕，由巴托尔迪正式赠送给美国人民。
[01:33.85]Ever since then, the great monument has been a symbol of liberty | 从那时起，这座伟大的纪念碑一直是自由的象征，
[01:39.32]for the millions of people who have passed through New York Harbour to make their homes in America. | 对于经过纽约港到美国安家的千百万移民来说尤其如此。
